Calculate the area of this irregular block of land.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\coordinate (A) at (0,0);
\coordinate (C) at (6.5,0);
\coordinate (B) at (2.2,2);
\coordinate (D) at (4.2,-2.75);
\coordinate (E) at (2.2,0);
\coordinate (F) at (4.2,0);
\draw[thick] (A) -- (B) -- (C) -- (D) -- cycle;
\draw[thick] (A) -- (C) node[pos=0.85, above] {$26\text{ m}$};
\draw[dashed] (B) -- (E) node[midway, left] {$8\text{ m}$};
\draw[dashed] (D) -- (F) node[midway, right] {$11\text{ m}$};
\draw (E) rectangle ++(0.25,0.25);
\draw (F) rectangle ++(-0.25,-0.25);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A field is surveyed along a baseline $AB$. The baseline is divided into segments of $12\text{ m}$, $16\text{ m}$, and $10\text{ m}$. Perpendicular offsets on one side are $8\text{ m}$ and $14\text{ m}$ as shown. What is the total area of the field?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\coordinate (A) at (0,0);
\coordinate (B) at (7.6,0);
\coordinate (X) at (2.4,0);
\coordinate (Y) at (5.6,0);
\coordinate (P) at (2.4,1.6);
\coordinate (Q) at (5.6,2.8);
\draw[thick] (A) -- (P) -- (Q) -- (B) -- cycle;
\draw[dashed] (P) -- (X) node[midway, left] {$8\text{ m}$};
\draw[dashed] (Q) -- (Y) node[midway, right] {$14\text{ m}$};
\node[below] at (1.2,0) {$12\text{ m}$};
\node[below] at (4,0) {$16\text{ m}$};
\node[below] at (6.6,0) {$10\text{ m}$};
\draw (X) rectangle ++(0.25,0.25);
\draw (Y) rectangle ++(0.25,0.25);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
